  "title": {
    "en": "Epoch handoff: what may change across epochs, what must not"
  },
  "kind": "theorem",
  "status": "recorded-checked",
  "statement": {
    "en": "Upgrades passing SwitchoverHandoffGate (or zero-draw EpochHandoffGate) keep the original floor and current guard over every run, even under nonzero switchover draw when post-switchover margin holds; timely pre-breach residual readouts admit unmodelled sites before floor breach refuses late entry."
  },
  "hypotheses": [
    {
      "en": "No axiom. RegimeMargin.Coupled.Indexed.Rises for G; EpochCert of the starting epoch; starting state in its K; lag margin x_crit + eta * (sitePreCap + envCap) <= x0 on in-scope sites. Non-deadlock: EpochTotal of the starting epoch and the starting state in K."
    }
  ],
